WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.788
The module challenge asks you to create one query
for a decision-maker

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:08.925
The question is which sales categories generated
meaningful revenue and how much

00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:14.225
did each qualifying category contribute Start with
the required grain one row

00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:19.800
per category That means category belongs in GROUP BY
You need at

00:00:19.825 --> 00:00:24.338
least two aggregate measures A useful pair could be
total quantity and

00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:29.325
total revenue although other reasonable measures may
also work The query must

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:33.525
include a row condition in WHERE This should
describe which source sale

00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:37.875
rows are allowed to participate It must also include
a group condition

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:43.712
in HAVING which should describe which completed
category summaries qualify Finally sort

00:00:43.725 --> 00:00:47.688
the result in a meaningful descending analytical
order such as highest revenue

00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:52.738
first After running the query write two short
sentences explaining the result

00:00:53.612 --> 00:00:57.875
One sentence should describe what the rows mean The
second should clearly

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.050
distinguish the WHERE row filter from the HAVING
group filter Do not

00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:06.462
treat this as a syntax puzzle Design the report from
the decision

00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:10.962
question If you can explain why each clause exists
the query is

00:01:10.988 --> 00:01:12.950
doing more than just running successfully
